>Basic Line Editor V1.3 by Tenaglia
     This editor works on the same principle as basic interpreter
     environments.  The lines are all prefixed with line numbers.
     These line numbers  are used to reference lines in the file.
     The line numbers are not written to, or read from  the file.
     This editor is designed to work on a hard copy terminal like
     a teletype or decwriter as well as a crt.
Command Summary : (parameters are space delimited)
  NEW       - erase buffer        | CLS        - clear screen or form feed
  LOAD file - load file           | SAVE file  - save file
  READ file - read w/line numbers | WRITE file - write w/line numbers
  RESAVE    - resave current file | MERGE file - insert w/line numbers
  DIR [spec]- list directory      | SIZE       - lines in editing buffer
  RENUM     - renumber the lines  | VER        - current version number
  COMPILE   - current source      | BUILD      - compile & link
  TEST      - compile,link, & run | RUN        - run last compiled
  $ - command to system (shell)   | HELP or ?  - this help screen
  TIME or DATE - displays time    | !!         - repeat last command
*---------------------------------+--------------------------------------*
  LIST or DEL [from [to]]  - list or delete line(s)
  FIND str [repl]  - find or replace string
  EXIT or QUIT     - return to operating system
>Returning to operating system
